Title: Meroe
Order: 12
Production Code: 1x12

EXT. MEROE - CAMP - NIGHT

AMB: the Nile moving past the camp, moonlight on ruins

The expedition has finally reached the outskirts of ancient Meroe. [[Professor Stone]] unseals a parchment he has carried for twenty-five years, given to him by a dying camel-driver.

PROFESSOR STONE
(reading, translating as he goes)
"Four days' journey toward Arabia, gold in bars and gold in flakes, diamonds hidden by the priests of Osiris, that adorned the crown of the royal line of Queen Candace..."

CHARLIE VANCE
Rubbish. What about the sacred crocodile and the jewel-crowned serpents you left out just now?

PROFESSOR STONE
The camel-driver told me one thing more, that isn't on the page. That from lands beyond the sea, where the descendants of Ethiopia were carried as slaves, a king of the ancient line — an heir of Ergamenes — would one day return and restore the hidden city's glory.

CHARLIE VANCE
And how would anyone know their own king after that many centuries, amalgamation and all?

PROFESSOR STONE
Every descendant of the line bears a lotus-lily birthmark on the breast.

[[Reuel Briggs]] starts, visibly, at the words — enough that Charlie notices, and says nothing.

REUEL BRIGGS
(quiet, to himself, unheard)
We'll prove whether there's a hidden city or not before we leave Africa.
